  {
   "id": "name",
   "text": "Meet Henry Johnson.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Henry Johnson",
    "sub": "1892-1929"
   },
   "section": "who"
  },
  {
   "id": "porter",
   "text": "A railroad porter from Albany, New York, he joined the Harlem Hellfighters in 1917.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "bearers",
    "caption": "Color bearers of the 15th New York, 1917"
   },
   "section": "story",
   "overlays": {
    "pin": {
     "label": "Albany",
     "sub": "New York"
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "france",
   "text": "The U.S. Army kept Black units out of combat, so the regiment was lent to France.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Lent to France",
    "sub": "March 1918"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "night",
   "text": "On May 15, 1918, he and Needham Roberts were on sentry duty at a small outpost.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "argonne",
    "focus": [
     0.5,
     0.5
    ],
    "zoom": [
     1,
     1.08
    ]
   },
   "overlays": {
    "stamp": "15 May 1918"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "raid",
   "text": "A German raiding party attacked. At least a dozen men.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "At least 12",
    "sub": "German raiders"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "fight",
   "text": "Roberts was badly wounded. Johnson threw every grenade he had. His rifle jammed, so he swung it like a club. Then he drew his knife.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "raid",
    "focus": [
     0.5,
     0.5
    ],
    "zoom": [
     1,
     1.08
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "save",
   "text": "He would not let them take Roberts prisoner. The raiders pulled back.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "pair",
    "caption": "Henry Johnson and Needham Roberts, 1918"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "wounds",
   "text": "He had been wounded twenty-one times.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "21",
    "sub": "wounds"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "croix",
   "text": "France gave him the Croix de Guerre.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "pairmedals",
    "caption": "Johnson and Roberts with the Croix de Guerre"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "home",
   "text": "His own army sent him home with papers that did not mention a single wound. No disability pay.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "returnhome",
    "focus": [
     0.42,
     0.35
    ],
    "zoom": [
     1.3,
     1.4
    ]
   },
   "section": "twist"
  },
  {
   "id": "death",
   "text": "He died in 1929, at thirty-six, with almost nothing.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "1929",
    "sub": "age 36"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "moh",
   "text": "In 2015, ninety-seven years after that night, he was awarded the Medal of Honor.",
